<title>CANADA: Quebec begins campaign against underground economy.</title>
<headline>Quebec begins campaign against underground economy.</headline>
<dateline>QUEBEC CITY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Quebec government said on Tuesday that it will spend C$30 million and hire 1,000 civil servants temporarily to fight the province's burgeoning underground economy and tax fraud.</p>
<p>At a press conference, Quebec officials said they expect to recoup C$313 million of revenues by the end of fiscal 1996/97 through the new special measures.</p>
<p>&quot;This day constitutes a new step by the government in its battle against the anti-social activity that fraud is,&quot; Quebec Finance Minister Bernard Landry told reporters.</p>
</text>
